the machine will be indistinguishable from a god
[8/?] this is why the church has been in a death spiral for 50 years
[9/?] and the state will seem indistinguishable from a mafia
[10/?] that's not to say we're not at risk of an orwellian state
[11/?] but rather an orwellian state will be impossible if we allow the next iteration of the internet to mature in its natural state
[12/?] we do not understand the internet; it is like our children or grandchildren
[13/?] I think it will be a great adventure

@jacob @repligate This is a very interesting thread. But it’s missing the crucial point of the Internet being a tool for control and manipulation. In fact it will make it easier than ever. If AI doesn’t kill us, the internet will.

I don’t believe there are any “natural laws” in society. That’s not to say I’m a social constructivist. I believe that a “natural state” exists in the minds of people.

